Initial release — what a branch spent

What a branch spent, on what, and who recorded it.

The category is a plain string, not an enum or a foreign key. The list grows,
and summaries group by whatever is on the record — so adding a category never
touches an expense already recorded, and never needs a migration.

Money is integer shillings everywhere. A float is refused at the boundary
rather than rounded, because a rounding that happens quietly is a rounding
nobody can audit.
